    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. Could you give some specific examples of foods that fall into each category? Like, what are some common high GI items vs low GI items I should look out for?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "High GI foods include items like white bread, sugary sodas, and plain potatoes, which digester very quickly and spike blood sugar. Conversely, low GI foods such as berries, whole grains, and legumes break down slowly, providing a more sustainable energy release. When managing diabetes, pairing these low GI choices with healthy fats or proteins can further help stabilize your blood glucose levels throughout the day.",
      "source": "target",
